@*
    Spec §13.2: the Tasks page. Holds the *effective* View - the saved one with the toolbar's own
    session overrides applied (§13.3) - and requeries on exactly three hubs, narrowed from Spec
    §13.2's full subscription list by corrections-B4 D11 item 9: TaskEvents.TasksReloaded,
    TaskEvents.TaskChanged and ViewStore.ViewsChanged. TaskActivity/TurnActivity/PresenceChanged/
    PersonaHealth.Changed feed the AI-reacting chip, which is D14's work.

    The effective View's Kind picks the List or the Board (§13.4; 12.4.i). Both open a Task into the
    detail drawer, which is still an empty slot showing only the clicked Task's id until TaskDetail
    lands (14.5.i); + New task is still a no-op EventCallback. The Board's column header changes a
    saved Board View through ViewStore (the page follows ViewsChanged) and anything else through
    ViewChanged (the effective View), and its "Edit columns…" opens the View editor at Columns.
    Below either view, one §13.12 empty state: "No tasks yet." when there are no Tasks at all, "No
    tasks match '{text}'." when only the search excludes everything, otherwise "No tasks match this
    View." with Reset filters, which drops the toolbar's overrides and the search (J43).

    The View editor drawer (§13.5) IS hosted here (corrections-B5 D13 item 7; 13.2.i, the only agent
    editing this file for that dispatch per corrections-B7's ordering, J42), for two triggers that
    are both about the page's own on-screen state rather than an arbitrary View: the Board's "Edit
    columns…" (12.4.i, opens at Columns) and /tasks/new, which opens it for a new View, detected
    from NavigationManager.Uri since that route's own @page template carries no ViewId to
    distinguish it from the bare /tasks case. An invalid View route (corrections-B7 §13.2 item 4)
    shows its ViewValidator reason and its own Edit View button, opening this same hosted drawer,
    never the "no longer exists" wording that only ever meant "no such id at all". Editing any OTHER
    View - including the one currently effective here, by name rather than by being on screen - goes
    through TaskViewNav's own separate ViewEditorDrawer instance instead, reached from that View's
    row menu in the sidebar (moved there from a standalone toolbar button, so any View can be edited
    or deleted from wherever the Human is in the app, not only while it happens to be the page open
    here).

    14.5.i (this dispatch, third page-wiring step, corrections-B7): the detail drawer now hosts a real
    TaskDetail (Mode=Panel) instead of the placeholder - opening a row/card, "+ New task" (the toolbar
    button) and switching between two already-open Tasks all go through
    ConfirmSwitchAsync, which calls the currently mounted TaskDetail's own ConfirmDiscardAsync before
    tearing it down (a fresh @key forces recreation, since TaskDetail only loads its Id/Draft once, in
    OnInitializedAsync - Cancel in that "Discard changes?" box leaves the current Task open).
    OverlayAutoClose reads detailHasPending, a field this page keeps current from TaskDetail's own
    HasPendingChanged (settled J58) - never a direct read of TaskDetail.HasPending, because TaskDetail
    changing its own pending does not, by itself, re-render this ancestor: a direct read could act on
    a stale "nothing pending" and let the drawer's overlay click silently discard a real edit (the bug
    J58 fixed). WakeToasts (renders nothing itself) and the page-header AiReactingChip - watching every
    Task in the current effective View, not narrowed by the search box - are D14's remaining work, per
    corrections-B5 D14 item 12.
*@

@page "/tasks"
@page "/tasks/{ViewId}"
@page "/tasks/new"
@page "/tasks/item/{TaskIdText}"
@implements IDisposable
@using System.Text.Json
@using Microsoft.Extensions.Options
@inject TaskStore Store
@inject TaskEvents Events
@inject ViewStore Views
@inject IOptions<TeamOptions> Options
@inject IJSRuntime JS
@inject ISnackbar Snackbar
@inject NavigationManager Navigation

<div class="tasks-page">
    <WakeToasts OnOpenTask="this.OnOpenTaskAsync" />
    @if (!this.Options.Value.Tasks.Enabled)
    {
        @* corrections-B4 D11 item 13: Tasks turned off shows only this notice. *@
        <MudAlert Severity="Severity.Info" role="status" Class="tasks-disabled-alert">Tasks are turned off.</MudAlert>
    }
    else if (this.invalidView is { } invalid)
    {
        @* corrections-B7 §13.2 item 4: an invalid View (parses, fails ViewValidator) shows its
           reason and an Edit View button - never "no longer exists", which means no such id at all. *@
        <MudAlert Severity="Severity.Warning" role="status" Class="tasks-invalid-view-alert">
            This View is invalid: @string.Join(" ", invalid.Problems)
        </MudAlert>
        <MudButton OnClick="@(() => this.OpenEditorFor(invalid.Id ?? this.ViewId ?? string.Empty))" Class="tasks-invalid-view-edit">Edit View</MudButton>
    }
    else if (this.viewNotFound)
    {
        <MudAlert Severity="Severity.Warning" role="status" Class="tasks-view-not-found-alert">
            That View no longer exists.
            <MudLink Href="/tasks">All Tasks</MudLink>
        </MudAlert>
    }
    else
    {
        <header class="tasks-header">
            <h1>@this.effectiveView.Name</h1>
            @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(this.effectiveView.Description))
            {
                <MudText Typo="Typo.body2" Class="mud-text-secondary tasks-description">@this.effectiveView.Description</MudText>
            }
            @if (this.HasOverrides)
            {
                <MudLink OnClick="this.ResetOverrides" Class="tasks-reset">Reset</MudLink>
            }
            <AiReactingChip Watched="this.WatchedTaskIds" />
        </header>

        @if (this.Views.LoadError is { } loadError)
        {
            @* Spec §13.12: the exact wording, with the parse error's own line/column and message. *@
            <MudAlert Severity="Severity.Error" role="alert" Class="tasks-views-load-error-alert">
                views.json could not be read (line @loadError.Line, column @loadError.Column): @loadError.Message. Views are read-only until the file is fixed; nothing has been lost.
            </MudAlert>
        }

        @if (this.Store.RejectedFiles.Count > 0)
        {
            @* Teammates.razor:32-48's precedent, with role="status" added per traps.md L22-27. *@
            <MudAlert Severity="Severity.Warning" role="status" Class="tasks-rejected-alert">
                <MudText Typo="Typo.subtitle2" Class="tasks-rejected-heading">Tasks that didn't load</MudText>
                <ul class="tasks-rejected-list">
                    @foreach (RejectedTaskFile rejected in this.Store.RejectedFiles)
                    {
                        <li class="tasks-rejected-item">
                            <span class="tasks-rejected-path">@rejected.Path</span>
                            <span class="tasks-rejected-reason">@rejected.Reason</span>
                        </li>
                    }
                </ul>
            </MudAlert>
        }

        <TaskToolbar EffectiveView="this.effectiveView" EffectiveViewChanged="this.OnEffectiveViewChangedAsync"
                     Search="@this.search" SearchChanged="this.OnSearchChangedAsync"
                     OnNewTask="this.OnNewTaskAsync" />

        IReadOnlyList<TaskItem> tasks = this.FilteredTasks(this.search);
        @if (this.effectiveView.Kind == ViewKind.List)
        {
            <TaskListView View="this.effectiveView" Tasks="tasks" Search="@this.search" OnOpenTask="this.OnOpenTaskAsync" OnCopyId="this.OnCopyIdAsync" />
        }
        else
        {
            <TaskBoard View="this.effectiveView" Tasks="tasks" Search="@this.search" OnOpenTask="this.OnOpenTaskAsync"
                       ViewChanged="this.OnEffectiveViewChangedAsync" OnEditColumns="this.OnEditColumnsClicked" OnCopyId="this.OnCopyIdAsync" />
        }

        @if (tasks.Count == 0)
        {
            @* Spec §13.12 empty states, one rendering below the List and the Board (corrections-B7 12.4 item 1).
               "No tasks yet." carries no button of its own: the toolbar's "+ New task" is right above it. *@
            <div class="tasks-empty">
                @if (this.Store.All.Count == 0)
                {
                    <MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Class="tasks-empty-message">No tasks yet.</MudText>
                }
                else if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(this.search) && this.FilteredTasks(null).Count > 0)
                {
                    <MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Class="tasks-empty-message">No tasks match '@this.search'.</MudText>
                }
                else
                {
                    <MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Class="tasks-empty-message">No tasks match this View.</MudText>
                    <MudButton Variant="Variant.Text" OnClick="this.ResetOverrides" Class="tasks-empty-action">Reset filters</MudButton>
                }
            </div>
        }

        @if (this.itemNotFoundText is not null)
        {
            @* Spec §13.13.3 step 1: an item-route id that is invalid or names no Task, over the last View. *@
            <MudAlert Severity="Severity.Warning" role="status" Class="tasks-item-not-found-alert">@this.itemNotFoundText</MudAlert>
        }

        <MudDrawer Open="this.detailOpen" OpenChanged="this.OnDetailOpenChanged" Anchor="Anchor.End" Variant="DrawerVariant.Temporary"
                   OverlayAutoClose="@(!this.detailHasPending)" Class="tasks-detail-drawer">
            <div @ref="this.detailResizeHandle" class="tasks-detail-resize-handle" role="separator" aria-orientation="vertical" aria-label="Resize Task detail panel"></div>
            @if (this.selectedTaskId is not null || this.selectedDraft is not null)
            {
                <TaskDetail @ref="this.detail" @key="this.DetailKey" Id="this.selectedTaskId" Draft="this.selectedDraft"
                            Mode="TaskDetailMode.Panel" OnClose="this.OnDetailClosed" HasPendingChanged="this.OnDetailHasPendingChanged" />
            }
        </MudDrawer>
    }

    <ViewEditorDrawer Open="this.editorOpen" OpenChanged="this.OnEditorOpenChanged" Id="@this.editorViewId" Section="this.editorSection" />
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>The route's View id segment - null for the bare <c>/tasks</c> and <c>/tasks/new</c> routes.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? ViewId { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The route's Task id segment for <c>/tasks/item/{TaskIdText}</c> (Spec §13.13.3) - null for every other route.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? TaskIdText { get; set; }

    private TaskView effectiveView = new() { Id = ViewStore.AllTasksId, Name = "All Tasks", Kind = ViewKind.List };
    private string? search;
    private bool viewNotFound;
    private InvalidView? invalidView;
    private string? itemNotFoundText;
    private bool detailOpen;
    private TaskId? selectedTaskId;
    private TaskDraft? selectedDraft;
    private TaskDetail? detail;
    private bool detailHasPending;
    private ElementReference detailResizeHandle;

    /// <summary>The <c>localStorage</c> key <c>huddleResize.attachDrawer</c> (app.js) remembers the detail panel's dragged width under.</summary>
    private const string DetailWidthStorageKey = "taskDetailPanelWidth";

    /// <summary>The detail panel's narrowest and widest drag-resized widths, in pixels - narrow enough to still fit the Panel-mode conflict rows' stacked layout (manual test TASKS-07 finding F17), wide enough to stay short of crowding the List/Board behind it on a typical laptop screen.</summary>
    private const int DetailWidthMinPx = 320;
    private const int DetailWidthMaxPx = 800;

    /// <summary>The detail panel's width before any drag has been recorded - matches <c>.tasks-detail-drawer</c>'s own CSS default in app.css, so a fresh browser (nothing in <c>localStorage</c> yet) renders the same width either way.</summary>
    private const int DetailWidthDefaultPx = 420;
    private bool editorOpen;
    private string? editorViewId;
    private ViewEditorSection editorSection = ViewEditorSection.General;

    /// <summary>Subscribes to the three hubs Spec §13.2 (narrowed by corrections-B4 D11 item 9) names.</summary>
    protected override void OnInitialized()
    {
        this.Events.TasksReloaded += this.OnTasksReloaded;
        this.Events.TaskChanged += this.OnTaskChanged;
        this.Views.ViewsChanged += this.OnViewsChanged;
    }

    /// <summary>Unsubscribes from all three hubs (rules.md: every component subscribing to a singleton hub must unsubscribe in Dispose).</summary>
    public void Dispose()
    {
        this.Events.TasksReloaded -= this.OnTasksReloaded;
        this.Events.TaskChanged -= this.OnTaskChanged;
        this.Views.ViewsChanged -= this.OnViewsChanged;
    }

    /// <summary>Resolves the effective View from the route's ViewId, then (Spec §13.13.3) the item route's <see cref="TaskIdText"/>, every time either changes.</summary>
    protected override async Task OnParametersSetAsync()
    {
        this.ResolveEffectiveViewFromRoute();
        await this.ResolveItemRouteAsync();
    }

    /// <summary>The View-resolution half of <see cref="OnParametersSetAsync"/> - unchanged from before the item route existed.</summary>
    private void ResolveEffectiveViewFromRoute()
    {
        if (this.ViewId is null)
        {
            // The bare /tasks and /tasks/new routes both default to All Tasks; OnAfterRenderAsync
            // below may still redirect the bare route to a remembered last View. /tasks/new carries
            // no ViewId of its own to tell the two apart, so the route itself is read from the URI.
            this.viewNotFound = false;
            this.invalidView = null;
            this.SetEffectiveViewFromStore(ViewStore.AllTasksId);
            if (this.IsTasksNewRoute())
            {
                this.editorViewId = null;
                this.editorOpen = true;
            }

            return;
        }

        TaskView? found = this.Views.Get(this.ViewId);
        if (found is not null)
        {
            this.viewNotFound = false;
            this.invalidView = null;
            this.effectiveView = found;
            return;
        }

        // corrections-B7 §13.2 item 4: an entry that parsed but failed ViewValidator is InvalidView,
        // not merely absent - it gets its own reason and an Edit View button, never "no longer exists".
        InvalidView? invalid = this.Views.InvalidViews.FirstOrDefault(v => string.Equals(v.Id, this.ViewId, StringComparison.Ordinal));
        if (invalid is not null)
        {
            this.viewNotFound = false;
            this.invalidView = invalid;
            return;
        }

        this.viewNotFound = true;
        this.invalidView = null;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Spec §13.13.3: parses <see cref="TaskIdText"/> and opens the named Task's panel, or - if the text
    /// is invalid or names no Task - sets <see cref="itemNotFoundText"/> to the exact wording instead.
    /// Switching away from a different already-open Task goes through <see cref="ConfirmSwitchAsync"/>
    /// first (corrections-B6 "D15.2" item 2), the same guard <see cref="OnOpenTaskAsync"/> uses.
    /// </summary>
    private async Task ResolveItemRouteAsync()
    {
        if (this.TaskIdText is not { } text)
        {
            this.itemNotFoundText = null;
            return;
        }

        if (!TaskId.TryParse(text, out TaskId parsed) || this.Store.Get(parsed) is null)
        {
            this.itemNotFoundText = $"No task {text}.";
            this.selectedTaskId = null;
            this.selectedDraft = null;
            this.detailOpen = false;
            return;
        }

        this.itemNotFoundText = null;
        if (this.detailOpen && this.selectedTaskId == parsed)
        {
            return;
        }

        if (!await this.ConfirmSwitchAsync())
        {
            return;
        }

        this.selectedDraft = null;
        this.selectedTaskId = parsed;
        this.detailHasPending = false;
        this.detailOpen = true;
    }

    /// <summary>Whether the current URL is the literal <c>/tasks/new</c> route, which carries no <see cref="ViewId"/> of its own to tell it apart from the bare <c>/tasks</c> route.</summary>
    private bool IsTasksNewRoute() =>
        this.Navigation.ToAbsoluteUri(this.Navigation.Uri).AbsolutePath.EndsWith("/tasks/new", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase);

    /// <summary>Opens the View editor drawer for <paramref name="id"/> (the invalid-View route's Edit View button).</summary>
    private void OpenEditorFor(string id)
    {
        this.editorViewId = id;
        this.editorSection = ViewEditorSection.General;
        this.editorOpen = true;
    }

    /// <summary>The Board's <i>Edit columns…</i>: opens the View editor for the effective View at its Columns section (corrections-B7 12.4 item 7).</summary>
    private void OnEditColumnsClicked()
    {
        this.editorViewId = this.effectiveView.Id;
        this.editorSection = ViewEditorSection.Columns;
        this.editorOpen = true;
    }

    /// <summary>Reflects the drawer's own chrome (backdrop, Escape) closing it.</summary>
    private void OnEditorOpenChanged(bool open) => this.editorOpen = open;

    /// <summary>
    /// Spec §13.9: on first render of the bare route, reads the remembered last View and navigates
    /// there if it still exists. The item route (Spec §13.13.3 step 2) reads the same remembered View
    /// to decide what renders under its panel, but never navigates - the URL stays on
    /// <c>/tasks/item/{TaskIdText}</c> until the panel closes. First render is also when the detail
    /// drawer's drag-to-resize handle is wired up (<c>huddleResize.attachDrawer</c>, app.js): the
    /// drawer itself is never re-created while this page lives - only its <see cref="TaskDetail"/>
    /// child is, per <see cref="DetailKey"/> - so one attach call is enough for the page's whole
    /// lifetime, and every width the handle drags to afterwards is set and remembered entirely in
    /// JS, with no further round trip through this method.
    /// </summary>
    protected override async Task OnAfterRenderAsync(bool firstRender)
    {
        if (firstRender)
        {
            await this.JS.InvokeVoidAsync(
                "huddleResize.attachDrawer",
                this.detailResizeHandle,
                DetailWidthStorageKey,
                DetailWidthMinPx,
                DetailWidthMaxPx,
                DetailWidthDefaultPx);
        }

        if (firstRender && this.ViewId is null && this.TaskIdText is null && this.Options.Value.Tasks.Enabled)
        {
            await this.TryNavigateToLastViewAsync();
            return;
        }

        if (firstRender && this.TaskIdText is not null && this.Options.Value.Tasks.Enabled)
        {
            await this.TryLoadLastViewForItemRouteAsync();
        }

        if (this.ViewId is not null && !this.viewNotFound && this.Options.Value.Tasks.Enabled)
        {
            await this.TryStoreLastViewAsync(this.ViewId);
        }
    }

    /// <summary>Whether the effective View differs from the one <see cref="ViewStore"/> has saved, ignoring <see cref="TaskView.Scope"/> (the Active/Closed toggle is page state only, per Spec §13.3 and <c>TaskToolbar</c>'s own <c>ShowSaveToView</c>).</summary>
    private bool HasOverrides
    {
        get
        {
            TaskView? saved = this.Views.Get(this.effectiveView.Id);
            if (saved is null)
            {
                return false;
            }

            TaskView forCompare = this.effectiveView with { Scope = saved.Scope };
            string effectiveJson = JsonSerializer.Serialize(forCompare, ViewJson.Options);
            string savedJson = JsonSerializer.Serialize(saved, ViewJson.Options);
            return !string.Equals(effectiveJson, savedJson, StringComparison.Ordinal);
        }
    }

    /// <summary>Discards the toolbar's session overrides, falling back to the saved View.</summary>
    private void ResetOverrides()
    {
        TaskView? saved = this.Views.Get(this.effectiveView.Id);
        if (saved is not null)
        {
            this.effectiveView = saved;
            this.search = null;
        }
    }

    /// <summary>The Tasks matching the effective View's scope and filter and <paramref name="searchText"/>, sorted per its Sort keys - recomputed on every render, so a requery after any of the three subscribed events shows straight away.</summary>
    /// <param name="searchText">The search to apply; <see langword="null"/> for none (to tell "the search matches nothing" from "the filters match nothing").</param>
    private IReadOnlyList<TaskItem> FilteredTasks(string? searchText)
    {
        IReadOnlyList<TaskItem> filtered = TaskQuery.Filter(
            this.Store.All,
            this.effectiveView.Scope,
            this.effectiveView.Filter,
            searchText,
            this.Options.Value.HumanName);
        return TaskQuery.Sort(filtered, this.effectiveView.Sort);
    }

    private void SetEffectiveViewFromStore(string id)
    {
        if (this.Views.Get(id) is { } view)
        {
            this.effectiveView = view;
        }
    }

    private Task OnEffectiveViewChangedAsync(TaskView view)
    {
        this.effectiveView = view;
        return Task.CompletedTask;
    }

    private Task OnSearchChangedAsync(string? value)
    {
        this.search = value;
        return Task.CompletedTask;
    }

    /// <summary>Opens the detail drawer's <see cref="TaskDetail"/> for the clicked row/card - a no-op when it is already showing that Task - guarded by <see cref="ConfirmSwitchAsync"/> (corrections-B7 14.5.i item 2).</summary>
    /// <param name="id">The clicked Task's id.</param>
    private async Task OnOpenTaskAsync(TaskId id)
    {
        if (this.detailOpen && this.selectedTaskId == id)
        {
            return;
        }

        if (!await this.ConfirmSwitchAsync())
        {
            return;
        }

        this.selectedDraft = null;
        this.selectedTaskId = id;
        this.detailHasPending = false;
        this.detailOpen = true;
    }

    /// <summary>"+ New task" (the header button, Spec §13.3): opens the drawer's <see cref="TaskDetail"/> in create mode with <paramref name="defaults"/>.</summary>
    /// <param name="defaults">The Team/Project the effective View's filter names, when it names exactly one.</param>
    private async Task OnNewTaskAsync(NewTaskDefaults defaults)
    {
        if (!await this.ConfirmSwitchAsync())
        {
            return;
        }

        this.selectedTaskId = null;
        this.selectedDraft = new TaskDraft(string.Empty, defaults.Team ?? string.Empty, defaults.Project);
        this.detailHasPending = false;
        this.detailOpen = true;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Asks the currently mounted <see cref="TaskDetail"/> (if any) to confirm discarding pending
    /// edits before this page switches what the drawer shows (corrections-B7 14.5.i item 2). With
    /// nothing mounted yet - the drawer has never been opened - there is nothing to discard.
    /// </summary>
    private Task<bool> ConfirmSwitchAsync() => this.detail is null ? Task.FromResult(true) : this.detail.ConfirmDiscardAsync();

    /// <summary>Closes the detail drawer (<see cref="TaskDetail.OnClose"/>): Cancel, a successful Close/Reopen, or returning from Expand.</summary>
    private void OnDetailClosed() => this.OnDetailOpenChanged(false);

    /// <summary>
    /// Reflects the drawer's own chrome (backdrop click, Escape) closing it, and <see cref="TaskDetail.OnClose"/>
    /// (Cancel, Close/Reopen, Expand) - both go through here. On the item route (Spec §13.13.3 step 4),
    /// closing also replaces the URL with <c>/tasks/{effectiveView.Id}</c>, so Back does not reopen the
    /// panel; the ordinary <c>/tasks</c>/<c>/tasks/{ViewId}</c> routes never change the URL on close.
    /// </summary>
    /// <param name="open">The drawer's new Open state.</param>
    private void OnDetailOpenChanged(bool open)
    {
        this.detailOpen = open;
        if (!open && this.TaskIdText is not null)
        {
            this.Navigation.NavigateTo($"/tasks/{this.effectiveView.Id}", replace: true);
        }
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Tracks <see cref="TaskDetail.HasPendingChanged"/> (settled J58): the drawer's own
    /// <c>OverlayAutoClose</c> reads <see cref="detailHasPending"/>, never <c>this.detail.HasPending</c>
    /// directly - <see cref="TaskDetail"/> changing its own <c>pending</c> does not, by itself,
    /// re-render this page, so a direct read could act on a stale "nothing pending" and let the
    /// overlay silently discard a real edit.
    /// </summary>
    /// <param name="hasPending">Whether <see cref="TaskDetail"/> now has an unsaved edit pending.</param>
    private void OnDetailHasPendingChanged(bool hasPending) => this.detailHasPending = hasPending;

    /// <summary>
    /// <see cref="TaskDetail"/> only loads its <see cref="TaskDetail.Id"/>/<see cref="TaskDetail.Draft"/>
    /// once, in its own <c>OnInitializedAsync</c> - changing those parameters on the same instance would
    /// not reload it. Keying on the target (the Task id, or the Draft instance itself for create mode)
    /// forces Blazor to tear down and recreate <see cref="TaskDetail"/> whenever the drawer switches to
    /// a different Task or a fresh create-mode Draft.
    /// </summary>
    private object DetailKey => this.selectedDraft is { } draft ? draft : this.selectedTaskId is { } id ? id : "tasks-detail-none";

    /// <summary>The ids of every Task in the current effective View (Spec §10.8), unnarrowed by the search box, for <see cref="AiReactingChip.Watched"/>.</summary>
    private IReadOnlyList<TaskId> WatchedTaskIds => this.FilteredTasks(null).Select(t => t.Id).ToList();

    private void OnTasksReloaded() => _ = this.DispatchAsync(() =>
    {
        this.StateHasChanged();
        return Task.CompletedTask;
    });

    private void OnTaskChanged(TaskChange change) => _ = this.DispatchAsync(() =>
    {
        this.StateHasChanged();
        return Task.CompletedTask;
    });

    private void OnViewsChanged() => _ = this.DispatchAsync(() =>
    {
        this.SetEffectiveViewFromStore(this.effectiveView.Id);
        this.StateHasChanged();
        return Task.CompletedTask;
    });

    /// <summary>Invokes <paramref name="action"/> on the renderer's synchronization context, swallowing the two exceptions a hub event racing component teardown can throw (§13.11).</summary>
    private async Task DispatchAsync(Func<Task> action)
    {
        try
        {
            await this.InvokeAsync(action);
        }
        catch (ObjectDisposedException)
        {
            // Circuit gone; nothing to render.
        }
        catch (InvalidOperationException)
        {
            // Renderer disposed mid-dispatch.
        }
    }

    private async Task TryNavigateToLastViewAsync()
    {
        string? lastViewId;
        try
        {
            lastViewId = await this.JS.InvokeAsync<string?>("huddleStorage.get", "huddle.tasks.lastView");
        }
        catch (JSDisconnectedException)
        {
            // Circuit gone; nothing to navigate.
            return;
        }
        catch (JSException)
        {
            // Storage inaccessible (e.g. a private window); stay on All Tasks.
            return;
        }

        if (lastViewId is not null && this.Views.Get(lastViewId) is not null)
        {
            this.Navigation.NavigateTo($"/tasks/{lastViewId}", replace: true);
        }
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// The item route's own half of Spec §13.9/§13.13.3 step 2: reads the same remembered last View,
    /// but only to decide what <see cref="effectiveView"/> renders under the panel - never navigates,
    /// since the URL stays on <c>/tasks/item/{TaskIdText}</c> until the panel closes.
    /// </summary>
    private async Task TryLoadLastViewForItemRouteAsync()
    {
        string? lastViewId;
        try
        {
            lastViewId = await this.JS.InvokeAsync<string?>("huddleStorage.get", "huddle.tasks.lastView");
        }
        catch (JSDisconnectedException)
        {
            // Circuit gone; nothing to render.
            return;
        }
        catch (JSException)
        {
            // Storage inaccessible (e.g. a private window); stay on All Tasks.
            return;
        }

        if (lastViewId is not null && this.Views.Get(lastViewId) is { } view)
        {
            this.effectiveView = view;
            this.StateHasChanged();
        }
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// The page's own copy path (corrections-B7 "15.2.i" item 2, J52): a Board card's or a List row's
    /// "Copy id" calls <c>huddleClipboard.copy</c> directly, with no other <c>await</c> before it (the
    /// Spec §13.13.1 warning), and shows the same success/warning toast as the detail header's button.
    /// </summary>
    /// <param name="id">The Task id to copy.</param>
    private async Task OnCopyIdAsync(TaskId id)
    {
        bool copied = await this.JS.InvokeAsync<bool>("huddleClipboard.copy", id.ToString());
        if (copied)
        {
            this.Snackbar.Add($"Copied {id}", Severity.Success, configure: null, key: "copy");
        }
        else
        {
            this.Snackbar.Add("Couldn't copy. The id is selected; press Ctrl+C.", Severity.Warning, configure: null, key: "copy");
        }
    }

    private async Task TryStoreLastViewAsync(string viewId)
    {
        try
        {
            await this.JS.InvokeVoidAsync("huddleStorage.set", "huddle.tasks.lastView", viewId);
        }
        catch (JSDisconnectedException)
        {
            // Circuit gone; nothing to persist.
        }
        catch (JSException)
        {
            // Storage inaccessible; the key is the only thing lost.
        }
    }
}
